      "publicId": "chal_coding_kfk_152",
      "name": "retry-and-dead-letter-routing",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Route failed orders through retry topics to a dead-letter topic",
      "description": "The courier-matcher's first version let a matching error escape `eachMessage`: one OrderPlaced without an address was retried forever and held up every order behind it on partition 5. The editor holds `src/failures.ts`: `onRecord`, called for every record of `orders.v1` and of the retry topics, and `routeFailure`, which picks where a failed record goes next. Their key blocks are missing, each marked by a `// [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that: a failure never stops the partition (the record is published onward and the consumer moves on); validation and schema errors go to `orders.v1.dlt` at once; timeout and unavailable errors go to `orders.v1.retry.30s` after the 1st failure, `orders.v1.retry.5m` after the 2nd and the dead-letter topic after the 3rd; every forwarded record carries `x-attempts`, `x-error` and, kept from its first failure, `x-original-topic`, `x-original-partition`, `x-original-offset` and `x-first-failed-at`. The runner replays a lunch rush second by second against an in-memory broker, with a poison order and an outage of the maps API.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "outcomes": [
        "consuming"
      ],
      "points": 40,
      "hints": [
        "Follow one record through three failures: which topic does it land in each time, what do its headers say, and does the consumer move to the next offset after each failure or stay where it is?",
        "Look at what the catch block does with the error, how `x-attempts` is read from the incoming headers (a record from a retry topic already has some), which headers must keep their first value (`??`), and which failure kinds skip the retry topics.",
        "A payment webhook consumer with retry topics `pay.retry.1m` and `pay.retry.10m`: `const tries = Number(h[\"x-tries\"] ?? \"0\") + 1; if (err.kind === \"signature\") return { topic: \"pay.dlt\", headers }; return { topic: RETRIES[tries - 1] ?? \"pay.dlt\", headers };` and in the handler `try { pay(record) } catch (e) { const next = route(record, e); publish(next.topic, { ...record, headers: next.headers }); }`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "typescript",
        "filePath": "src/failures.ts",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
